### [from_formula()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}

::: {.doc-subject}

Parse a formula response such as `"Surv(time, status == 2)"`.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/main/greenwood/_outcome.py#L609-L654){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
from_formula(formula)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

The response is a call to `Surv()` or `event_time()`, with the arguments R's functions
take: `Surv(time, time2, event, type=, origin=)` and `event_time(time, status, time_max)`.
Arguments are column names and the expressions listed under `Outcome`. Column names that
aren't valid Python identifiers are quoted with backticks, and dotted R names such as
`ph.ecog` work without quoting.
:::

#### Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[formula]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The response, optionally followed by `~ 1`. To include covariates, pass the full
    formula to an estimator's `fit()` instead.
:::

#### Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Outcome]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A data-free description of the response.
:::

#### Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#3f4c3c4c .cell execution_count=8}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

gw.Outcome.from_formula(formula="Surv(time, status == 2)")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=8}
```
Outcome.surv(time='time', event='status == 2')
```
:::
:::


R's other forms work too:

::: {#1ad60992 .cell execution_count=9}
``` {.python .cell-code}
gw.Outcome.from_formula(formula="Surv(tstart, tstop, status %in% c(1, 2))")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=9}
```
Outcome.surv(time='tstart', time2='tstop', event='status in (1, 2)')
```
:::
:::


::: {#07ee251c .cell execution_count=10}
``` {.python .cell-code}
gw.Outcome.from_formula(formula="event_time(time, code, upper)")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=10}
```
Outcome.event_time(time='time', status='code', time_max='upper')
```
